  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-29T21:20:31.670Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the way malicious players are stealing avatars by ID, maybe it could be mitigated by allowing avatars to be private at the database level? You could set the toggle when uploading.\n\nAvatar change requests could be denied by the server if the requesting player doesn't match the owner, or clients could refuse to load a player's avatar if they're not the owner",
